Z||000018||chester||10-24-2001||06:51 AM||||Was that the rev limiter you where slamming?  Where's the smoke?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Once I get my driveway paved I'm going to do some burnout videos of my own  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Rob D<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigline.jpg">   <BR>Modified 2.8<BR>2.5" Drop<BR>11" Brakes<BR>17" Revolutions<BR>RCC Coilover Suspension||||reg||1
Z||000019||LT1 Chop Top||10-24-2001||06:49 PM||||First of all...thanks for the compliments.  I will try to answer all the questions as accurately as I can. <P> 1.  The exhaust it totally custom.  It took two days in the shop to have it done.  I replaced the older cats with newer, more free flowing cats, and some of the 'bends' were smoothed out.  There are two cats per bank with four tips (Corvette I think).  Dual exhaust I suppose.<P> 2. Several people asked about the 'rev-limiter.'  First of all, it came with the car.  And to answer MinnGreen....I am not positive why it is there.  It isn't kicking in LOW however, the tires were probably spinning at 70mph there!  I can only assume the limiter is there to keep me from blowing it up.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P> 3.  What gear can I spin the tires through?  3rd, easily, even when I am running under normal speed and 'hit it' too hard.  That is one of the dangers of a car this powerful.....a 180 spin happens before you know it!  I have not tried to spin the tires into 4th....3rd is scary enough for me.<P> 4. To answer Batt, as to how much is into the car, probably well over $25k including everything Archie did, and I have done.<P> 5. Where is the smoke?  Look carefully, its there. (low res vid)<P>I was actually partially on the shoulder of the road there, a bit uneven, you cannot tell very well from the angle, but the back end slid toward the left quite a bit.  Which is why I didn't slam into 2nd and keep the tires going.<P>Thanks again for the compliments and emails, over 400 hits in 2 days...far out.||||reg||1
Z||000020||artherd||10-25-2001||05:07 AM||||(looking at your car again)  God, I really love the look of the Choped Top GT...  so smooth, so EXOTIC!  <P>Hrm, sorry, I got drool on your car (again) I gotta get me one of these!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Hrm2, so there are just a total of four Catalysts and some exhaust tips?!  Wooowie!  Any silencers at all?  I would KILL for some pics  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I love the sound in the clip, can't imagine it in person, how do you like it?<P>PS: Yeah, hard to tell, but they tyres are totally spinning all the way through first, all the way off that rev limiter  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  <P>What tyres have you got on there now, you might consider stickier rubber (3rd gear?!?!?! ZOIKES MAN! YES YES I LOVE IT!!)<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by LT1 Chop Top:<BR><B>First of all...thanks for the compliments.  I will try to answer all the questions as accurately as I can. <P> 1.  The exhaust it totally custom.  It took two days in the shop to have it done.  I replaced the older cats with newer, more free flowing cats, and some of the 'bends' were smoothed out.  There are two cats per bank with four tips (Corvette I think).  Dual exhaust I suppose.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000021||LT1 Chop Top||10-25-2001||05:18 PM||||Atherd,<P>No...only two cats, one for the front bank and one for the rear bank.  I really like the sound, it is completely different than any other car I have heard.  No silencers.  I have an mpeg of my 88 doing a burn out too (well...squeeling really) and the supertrapps are COMPLETELY different in sound.  The tires are Dunlop Sport 8000.  They are not very sticky, but they have been lit up quite a bit.  What would you recommend?||||reg||2
Z||000022||KissMySSFiero||10-25-2001||07:07 PM||||Too Loud!!!!  wait wait...too fast...wait...ohdamn what am i saying.  im just jealous!!!<P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE Aol:SSFiero <BR>88FORMULA<BR>       <A HREF="mailto:SSFiero@Aol.com">SSFiero@Aol.com</A>        <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000023||artherd||10-26-2001||01:32 AM||||Wow, sounds *GREAT* and is emmisions legal (and just plain non-stinky) too!   I might have to try just such a setup for the Northstar car...<P>Tyre wise, you can't go wrong with a set of Pirelli Pzero Asymetricos.  Sticky/Grippy as all hell, and no compromises.  Get 'em as wide as your wheels (17x7.5 unless I miss my guess?  try 245/40/17) <A HREF="http://www.tirerack.com/tires/pirelli/pi_pzero.jsp" TARGET=_blank>http://www.tirerack.com/tires/pirelli/pi_pzero.jsp</A>  <A HREF="http://www.tirerack.com/tires/Compare1.jsp?startIndex=0&width=245%2F&ratio=40&diameter=17&search=true&pagelen=20&pagenum=1&pagemark=1&do=Search&manufacturer=Pirelli" TARGET=_blank>http://www.tirerack.com/tires/Compare1.jsp?startIndex=0&width=245%2F&ratio=40&diameter=17&search=true&pagelen=20&pagenum=1&pagemark=1&do=Search&manufacturer=Pirelli</A> <P>(I have some Dunlop Sport W10 tyres on the T-top car now, only 215/45/17, they stick fairly well, but it's just a lowly 2.8....  I like how they handle though, and their traditional Dunlop flat sidewalls  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P><BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by LT1 Chop Top:<BR><B>Atherd,<P>No...only two cats, one for the front bank and one for the rear bank.  I really like the sound, it is completely different than any other car I have heard.  No silencers.  I have an mpeg of my 88 doing a burn out too (well...squeeling really) and the supertrapps are COMPLETELY different in sound.  The tires are Dunlop Sport 8000.  They are not very sticky, but they have been lit up quite a bit.  What would you recommend?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
