Z||000025||SLYGUY||10-27-2001||09:24 PM||||artherd...<P>How can that be emissions legal?<BR>I didn't know that a Corvette V8 was ever available in a Fiero.<BR>The tree huggers up at the DMV in Sacramento would never approve of such a great car.<BR>I hope I'm right, but I thought that the car could only have the engine if it was in fact available in the car the year that it was produced.<P>The VIN would say V6, and the sniffer would see V8. Right?<P>Give us the goods.....<P>Sly||||reg||1
Z||000026||artherd||10-28-2001||01:57 AM||||Gotta register it in another state (think PO box, maildrop, etc  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  With that state's tags on it.<P>CA Smog is on the one hand good (2-year exam peroids, get RID of stinky cars) and on the other hand just terrible (The Northstar is going to be far cleaner than any fiero engine, peroid. yet they ban it.)<P>PS: it's only because the Northstar never came in any cars *with manual trannys* that it cannot pass.  They won't even consider it.  If I wussed out and used the automatic (HAH!~) I would be 'ca legal'<P>.....<P>Best!<BR>Ben<P><BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by SLYGUY:<BR><B>artherd...<P>How can that be emissions legal?<BR>I didn't know that a Corvette V8 was ever available in a Fiero.<BR>The tree huggers up at the DMV in Sacramento would never approve of such a great car.<BR>I hope I'm right, but I thought that the car could only have the engine if it was in fact available in the car the year that it was produced.<P>The VIN would say V6, and the sniffer would see V8. Right?<P>Give us the goods.....<P>Sly</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
