Z||000029||westtexas||10-28-2001||02:40 PM||||That is an outstanding car and the exhaust sound is second to none. Would $10,000 get an Archie kit, new engine, FI harness, exhaust, and extras to duplicate your driveline? I drove a used '98 Trans Am this weekend. The sound alone would keep me in trouble. That sharp, crackling sound is just too good to leave alone. Is the San Antonio club having a meet or anything happening this Fall/winter where I could see your car in person?<P>Your chop top is lighter, cheaper, more exotic than a Trans Am. The only thing I can say in defense of my 4.9 swap is that it won't be so powerful that it swaps ends in third. I'll put the same exhaust in my car, hope for a similar sound. <P>I sure would like the 3.8 drivers to record their exhaust for comparison purposes.<P>Thanks for enlightening me (sigh),<BR>Robert<P><p>[This message has been edited by westtexas (edited 10-28-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000030||westtexas||10-28-2001||03:43 PM||||LT1, how about this idea. You have your brother in the car with a video camera, cruise around some good hill country roads recording the sights and sounds (perhaps passing a few slower cars) and some of us 'wannabes' pay you for copies. I could listen to that motor for hours, central Texas is beautiful. I would pay $20. It would be better than a new DVD. Anybody else interested in buying? You could limit the copies to 20 or 30. Your burnout is just a teaser. Imagine going out into the shop and listening to your favorite sound as you work on your Fiero! Or watching the video as you read the Fiero shop manual/latest Kit Car.<P>In the empty flatlands of Texas,<BR>Robert||||reg||1
Z||000031||LT1 Chop Top||10-29-2001||05:41 PM||||WestTexas,<P>We just had an AAFO meeting last weekend, sorry to have you miss it!  We meet the last Sunday of every month.<P>Here is our club page: <A HREF="http://communities.msn.com/AlamoAreaFieroOwners/_whatsnew.msnw" TARGET=_blank>http://communities.msn.com/AlamoAreaFieroOwners/_whatsnew.msnw</A> <P>As for the video....Ill have to think about that.  I can't imagine that there is much of a market for it.<P>I do have some more Mpegs of the car I could email to you if you are interested (as long as you don't mind BIG downloads)||||reg||1
Z||000032||westtexas||10-29-2001||09:17 PM||||LT1, well, I may be an audience of one. I once bought a video tape of a guy flying a hang glider on a two hour flight in Florida. I did give me an idea of what it's like to sit high in the sky for awhile. I would like to have your other MPEG's. If they'll make it past my ISP, I don't care if they are long downloads. I'll send my email by PM.<P>Do you cruise at night in San Antonio? When I was a kid (the sun was small and there was no moon then) San Antone was wild after midnight.<P>Thanks,<BR>Robert||||reg||1
